# AvaKit eERC project rules

Register, mint, and privately transfer tokens with hidden balances using Avalanche's Encrypted ERC standard.

## Flow

- Init: `useEERC(publicClient, walletClient, EERC_CONTRACT_ADDRESS, circuits)` — `circuits` is
  `await loadVerifiedCircuits()` from `lib/eerc-config.ts` (downloads the pinned circuit files,
  verifies each against a pinned SHA-256, returns blob URLs; never hand the SDK raw CDN URLs).
- Register (one-time, on-chain, idempotent): `eerc.register()`.
- Unlock (per session, off-chain, free): `eerc.generateDecryptionKey()`.
- Balance/actions: `eerc.useEncryptedBalance()` → `privateMint` (owner-only), `privateTransfer`, `privateBurn`.

## Wallet client

`@avakit/core`'s `getWalletClient` does not attach an `account`, but the eERC SDK requires
`wallet.account.address` to be set. Build the wallet client directly:
`createWalletClient({ chain: toViemChain(chain), transport: custom(provider), account: address })`.

## Amounts

- The token has 2 decimals (read `balance.decimals`, don't hardcode). Always convert with
  `parseUnits` / `formatUnits`.

## Contract

- No bundled `contracts/` — the eERC contracts are under Ava Labs' Ecosystem License (not MIT),
  so they are never vendored here. The template points at a shared, pre-deployed standalone
  instance on Fuji; `privateMint` is `onlyOwner`, so to mint run
  `DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=0x... pnpm deploy:eerc` (clones the official repo pinned to the
  circuits' commit, deploys YOUR instance, rewrites `lib/eerc-config.ts`), then connect the
  deployer wallet and complete the one-click "Set auditor" step the UI shows.

## Test AVAX

- On Fuji, `app/providers.tsx` passes `faucetUrl` to `<AvaKitProvider>`: the temporary wallet is
  funded when it connects, any other empty wallet through `useFaucet().fund()`. The default is
  AvaKit's shared Fuji faucet: rate-limited (one small drip per address per day, plus an hourly cap
  per IP address), paid for by the AvaKit maintainer, for first runs only — not for a product.
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_AVAKIT_FAUCET_URL` = your own faucet's `/fund` URL (Worker in `services/faucet` of
  the AvaKit repository), or `off`. Never pass a faucet URL on a chain other than Fuji.
- `components/funding.tsx` (`useFunding()`, `<FundingNotice />`) shows the funding state and the
  fallback (the official faucet needs a free Builder Hub sign-in). Disable transaction buttons only
  while `funding.isEmpty` — an unknown balance is not an empty one.
- Never call `fund()` on mount: the provider already asks for the temporary wallet and reports it
  through `useFaucet()`, and a second request is refused as "funded recently". `status: "success"`
  means the faucet sent the drip, not that it arrived — wait for a non-zero balance.

## UI & safety

- shadcn/ui only; black & white for now; dark/light via next-themes; both must work.
- Animations: Framer Motion or GSAP only.
- Registering/minting/transferring/burning cost gas (except unlocking); a new wallet is funded by the
  faucet (see "Test AVAX").
- Fuji only: the shared eERC instance and `pnpm deploy:eerc` both live on Fuji. Do not switch the
  chain in `app/providers.tsx` — on any other chain there is no eERC contract at
  `EERC_CONTRACT_ADDRESS`.
- wagmi is pinned to 2.x (not the latest major) because `@avalabs/eerc-sdk` peer-depends on `^2.0.0`.
